<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a modular belt conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A modular belt conveyor uses interlocking plastic modules connected by hinge rods to form the conveying surface. Unlike one-piece fabric belts, modular belts consist of individual segments that snap together and can be replaced individually if damaged. See our <a href="/conveyor-types/flat-belt-conveyors/">flat belt conveyor guide</a> for comparison.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What are the advantages of modular belt over flat belt?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Modular belts offer field-repairable construction, curve capability with radius-rated series, superior chemical resistance for washdown environments, and a wide range of surface patterns. Flat belts cost less and provide smoother, quieter operation for delicate products.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Can modular belt conveyors handle curves?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Yes, with a radius-rated belt series. Modules articulate at hinge points, allowing the belt to follow curved paths without tracking issues. Minimum inside turn radius is a multiple of belt width set by the series. Intralox lists 2.2 times belt width for its Series 2200 Radius Flush Grid and 1.7 to 2.2 times belt width, depending on width, for its Series 2400 Tight Turning Radius belt.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What should I look for when choosing a modular belt supplier?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Evaluate module geometry options for your product, material compatibility with your washdown chemistry and temperature range, local spare parts availability, and whether the belt pitch and hinge rod design are cross-compatible with your existing frames. Several global suppliers offer proprietary designs, so confirm that replacement modules and sprockets are stocked regionally.</p>

</div>
</div>
